# Copy this file to .env and adjust for your environment:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Expo reads EXPO_PUBLIC_* variables natively at build time (no extra package
# needed, supported since Expo SDK 49) — see src/config/env.ts.
#
# No secrets belong in this file, ever: everything prefixed EXPO_PUBLIC_ is
# bundled into the client app and is NOT private. Never put a JWT secret,
# database credential, or PayMongo secret key here — those are backend-only
# concerns (see backend/.env.example) and have no reason to exist in a mobile
# app bundle.

# Backend API base URL. Local dev backend defaults to http://localhost:4000
# (backend/README.md §5). Point this at your backend's actual address when
# testing on a physical device (localhost won't resolve to your dev machine
# from a phone on the same network — use your machine's LAN IP instead, e.g.
# http://192.168.1.23:4000).
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:4000
